From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nftables: serialize port allocations with fw4 reservations

Coordinate OpenWrt timed port triggers and native UPnP/NAT-PMP/PCP mappings
through the existing fw4 lock and one bounded reservation snapshot. Treat
a missing reservation set as ordinary firewall4 compatibility; reject an
incomplete or malformed set rather than allocate a conflicting mapping.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/commonrdr.h
+++ b/commonrdr.h
@@ -12,6 +12,26 @@
  */
 
 #include "config.h"
+
+/* A request holds the fw4 configuration lock from its reservation snapshot
+ * through mapping publication. Begin/end may nest within one daemon request.
+ * Only startup lease restoration may wait; event-loop requests fail if busy.
+ * A successful begin permits O(1) reserved-port lookup until the matching end.
+ * The OpenWrt producer owns inet fw4 port_trigger_ports and /var/run/fw4.lock.
+ * Set keys concatenate ifname, inet_proto and inet_service; nftables pads each
+ * component to a 32-bit register boundary, with network-order protocol/port.
+ * An absent set is ordinary fw4 compatibility; invalid/incomplete dumps fail.
+ */
+#ifdef USE_NFTABLES
+int port_mapping_begin(const char *ifname, int wait);
+void port_mapping_end(void);
+int port_mapping_reserved(unsigned short port, int proto);
+#else
+static inline int port_mapping_begin(const char *ifname, int wait) { (void)ifname; (void)wait; return 0; }
+static inline void port_mapping_end(void) {}
+static inline int port_mapping_reserved(unsigned short port, int proto)
+{ (void)port; (void)proto; return 0; }
+#endif
 
 /* init and shutdown functions */
 
